1
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on peace
and stepping away from it.

2
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:26,900
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:33,980
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,340
Would you put me in a chokehold, I wonder?

5
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed at me for staying a kid.

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
a sudden sigh, a yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,480
From the pointed-hat water bottle,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,800
under the great sky, the sun sets.

11
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,360
In Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness is lost again.

13
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,040
Because I'm a fool who only realized it.

14
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,120
Congratulations.

15
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:24,960
Congratulations.

16
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,620
Congratulations.

17
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,200
Congratulations.

18
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:27,220
Congratulations.

19
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:27,240
Congratulations.

20
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:27,280
Congratulations.

21
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:27,300
Congratulations.

22
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:27,320
Congratulations.

23
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,580
Congratulations.

24
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:29,440
Congratulations.

25
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:29,860
Congratulations.

26
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:30,340
Congratulations.

27
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:30,980
Well, well, look who it is, Ryotsu.

28
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,680
Listen, no matter what happens,
don't you dare let go of Maria!

29
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,780
Got it, Chief.

30
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:41,220
Ryo-sama, I'm so happy it's almost scary.

31
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,700
Same here, you know.

32
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:44,680
Ryo-sama...

33
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:46,560
Maria...

34
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:55,080
Maria, what on earth are you wearing?!

35
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:55,875
Oh my,

36
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:59,800
A real man looks best in a fundoshi loincloth,
after all!

37
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:00,740
A man?

38
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,480
Damn it! Maria is a man!

39
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,987
Ryo-sama! From you, Ryo-sama, I

40
00:03:10,037 --> 00:03:11,780
will never leave your side
for the rest of my life!

41
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:15,640
Stop! Let go! Stop! Let go! Help!

42
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:22,820
What, it was a dream...

43
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,020
Are you awake already?

44
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,720
Good morning, Ryo-sama.

45
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:58,140
There, it's ready.

46
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,420
Ryo-sama, let's have breakfast.

47
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:07,620
Here you are.

48
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:09,880
Itadakimasu.

49
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:10,620
There, there.

50
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,180
I ate so much.

51
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,100
Here you go, Ryo-san.

52
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:35,160
Was the miso soup too salty?

53
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,480
No, it was just right.

54
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:40,400
How about the pickles?
Did you like them? I made them myself.

55
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:41,740
Yeah, they were good.

56
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,619
I'm glad.
I'm so happy that Ryo-sama enjoyed them,

57
00:04:45,669 --> 00:04:47,520
I'm really delighted.

58
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:57,120
That's not right! Why are you in my room?!

59
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:01,540
Is it not allowed?
Me living together with Ryo-sama?

60
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,420
Of course it's not allowed!

61
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:07,520
Why not? Why is it not allowed, Ryo-sama?

62
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:08,860
It's

63
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:09,880
It's

64
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,580
because you're a man, Maria!

65
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,580
That's so cruel, Ryo-sama.

66
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:26,620
Cruel? Why on earth would I have to
live a newlywed life with a man like you?

67
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:32,560
Actually,
I consulted Komachi-san and Naoko-san.

68
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:38,720
It's been over a year since I met Ryo-sama,
and we haven't made any progress at all?

69
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:43,140
What can I do to make Ryo-sama
understand my feelings?

70
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:46,420
You really like that caveman that much?

71
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:47,654
Of course,

72
00:05:47,704 --> 00:05:52,840
whenever I think of Ryo-sama, my heart feels like it's going to burst.
It aches and hurts so much.

73
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:56,720
No offense to Maria-chan,
but we just don't get it.

74
00:05:57,100 --> 00:06:00,900
Seriously,
what on earth do you see in a guy like that?

75
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:04,660
Everything! He's manly and resourceful,

76
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:07,100
short-legged and big-faced,

77
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,000
stingy as an old man and disgustingly crude,

78
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,500
self-centered and money-grubbing,

79
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,900
and that rotten gay
bastard with the unibrow,

80
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:18,960
the octopus bastard who's been number one on the
"men you'd never want to marry" survey, year after year!

81
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,660
Please be serious.

82
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:32,740
I'm really agonizing over this.

83
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:40,160
Ways to make a man make up his mind

84
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:43,120
I guess we just have to go
with the classic approach.

85
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,080
Classic?

86
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,300
Like cooking him a home-cooked meal.

87
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:55,620
Or you could just go all out and barge in on him yourself. Yeah, that's the
"showing up uninvited" move.

88
00:06:56,120 --> 00:07:02,540
Maybe if you go for it, he'll forget
Maria is a man and end up falling for her.

89
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:06,480
Like, you do this and that,
and keep pushing, that's the way.

90
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,660
Alright, I'll give it a try.

91
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,060
That's how it is, darling.

92
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:17,680
Those idiots filled her head with nonsense.

93
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:24,270
Ryo-sama, though it's only for two days,

94
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:26,360
I humbly ask for your kindness.

95
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,000
Here you go, Ryo-sama. Your bento.

96
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:36,980
Have a good day!
Please come home early, okay?

97
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,820
Well, Maria's been playing the devoted wife

98
00:07:57,820 --> 00:08:00,480
Yeah, it's really a problem, I swear.

99
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,700
Wow, what a cute bento!

100
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,740
It's overflowing with love, this one.

101
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:09,620
Ryo-chan,
why don't you finally make up your mind?

102
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:16,480
Of course I have, I'm prepared to get married, Ryo-tsu!
Chief, you know that too, right?

103
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:25,360
Maria is a man, you know. But Maria-chan is more ladylike than any real girl.
That's right, senpai, the way Maria-san devotes herself to you day after day.

104
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:33,020
It's touching to watch. A woman willing to become your bride,
Ryo-chan, comes along maybe once in a hundred years.

105
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:35,020
Once in a hundred years?
It's not a comet, you know!

106
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,860
No, this is a once-in-a-lifetime chance,
you know.

107
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:40,040
Ryotsu, don't worry about the small details.

108
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,156
I'm willing to do it too, since we're at it.

109
00:08:41,206 --> 00:08:44,940
I was thinking I could even serve as a
groomsman at a wedding between two men.

110
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:49,140
Don't be ridiculous! I haven't the
slightest intention of anything like that.

111
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,220
Ryo-san.

112
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:55,480
Plum.

113
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,660
He finally got married, you know.

114
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:58,300
Whoa!

115
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,520
Who's the idiot spreading that nonsense?!

116
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:03,260
W-wasn't it the girl from Minipoto?

117
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:06,440
It was Aoko from Komachi-chō
Those guys are saying way too much.

118
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,360
I heard Ryo-chan got himself a bride, right?

119
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,060
I keep telling you, it's not like that.

120
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:15,540
Ryo-sama, Ryo-sama, Maria is so...

121
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:19,020
Fancy meeting you here, Ryo-sama!

122
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:23,080
Surely we're bound together by the red string of fate,
aren't we?

123
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:26,140
Don't be so dramatic,
it's nothing like that.

124
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:30,060
Come on,
you did get married after all, Ryo-san!

125
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:31,860
You're just embarrassed.

126
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,180
Isn't that Maria-chan from the police box?

127
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:36,140
She's too good for you, Ryo-san.

128
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:38,140
I already told you, it's not like that!

129
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:40,280
What's wrong with it, Ryo-sama?

130
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:41,280
It's not okay.

131
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:43,300
Maria, never mind,
come over here for a second.

132
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,620
Alright, then, goodbye everyone.

133
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,680
Take care of Ryo-san, ma'am.

134
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:49,260
Congratulations, and be happy.

135
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,960
Listen, Maria.

136
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,920
Just because we ran into each
other in the same neighborhood,

137
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,200
don't go hugging me every time.

138
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,960
Sorry, Ryo-sama.

139
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,040
I just got so happy.

140
00:09:57,660 --> 00:10:00,180
By the way, Ryo-sama,
you like sukiyaki, don't you?

141
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:00,840
Sukiyaki?

142
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:05,024
I want you to get some stamina from me,
Ryo-sama,

143
00:10:05,074 --> 00:10:07,300
so I went and bought
ingredients for sukiyaki.

144
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,580
Please come home early today, okay?

145
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:12,571
Sukiyaki It's been a
while since I've had it.

146
00:10:12,621 --> 00:10:14,220
Make sure you have beer ready too.

147
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,580
Okay! I'll be waiting for your return,
Ryo-sama.

148
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,620
I told you not to hug me!

149
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:20,660
Okay.

150
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:21,773
Uh-oh.

151
00:10:21,823 --> 00:10:25,760
I feel like I've totally
fallen into Maria's rhythm.

152
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:32,220
Hey, little miss,
what do you see in a wimp like this?

153
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:34,660
Forget about this guy and come with us.

154
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:36,740
We'll take you somewhere fun, alright?

155
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:41,780
You're super hot, you know.
You're too good for a guy like him.

156
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:44,600
You punk!

157
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:46,300
Shut up!

158
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,060
Ryo-sama, don't look!

159
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:49,160
Yay!

160
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:55,360
Hey, you!

161
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:09,760
Hey, Ryo-chan!

162
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:11,680
You've caused trouble again.

163
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:15,440
I got called in by the Chief
and chewed out because of you!

164
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,920
That wasn't me, it was Maria -

165
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:18,920
Shut up!

166
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:21,580
Maria is your wife, isn't she?

167
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,540
A wife's responsibility is
her husband's responsibility.

168
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,380
You haven't been supervising her properly.

169
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,820
This is ridiculous.

170
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:31,080
Listen! If you're married, act like a
married couple and properly educate Maria!

171
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:32,980
I already told you, we're not married!

172
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:37,442
On top of getting a three-hour lecture,

173
00:11:37,492 --> 00:11:39,500
I have to write a report.
I can't take this anymore.

174
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:43,540
This is all Maria's fault.
I should have put my foot down with her.

175
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:47,333
Ugh, this is unbearable, unbearable.

176
00:11:47,383 --> 00:11:48,959
I can't take it.

177
00:11:49,009 --> 00:11:51,720
Unbearable... when I think about it.

178
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,398
Welcome home, Ryo-sama.

179
00:11:58,448 --> 00:12:01,560
Would you like a bath?
Or would you prefer to eat first?

180
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,540
The sukiyaki is ready, but...

181
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:06,440
Sukiyaki! Food! Eat first!

182
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:07,440
Coming!

183
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:13,860
Whoa! Hehe!
Sukiyaki, sukiyaki, I'm so happy!

184
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,672
Ryo-sama,

185
00:12:15,722 --> 00:12:18,780
before that,
there's something I'd like you to look at.

186
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,400
What is it?

187
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:22,600
What is it?

188
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,720
I knitted this so we could wear matching outfits,
Your Majesty.

189
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:29,580
Cut it out. There's no way
I'm wearing something like this.

190
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,860
Why not?

191
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,380
If two men wore something like this,
it'd look weird!

192
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:36,217
"Men, men," that's all you ever say,
Your Majesty.

193
00:12:36,267 --> 00:12:38,760
Don't be so picky about little details.

194
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:39,640
It's not a little detail!

195
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,218
That's right, Maria.
You're undeniably a man.

196
00:12:43,268 --> 00:12:45,220
And you have a ridiculous
amount of strength, too.

197
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,700
Because of that,
I've been put through a lot of trouble.

198
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,420
Trouble?

199
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:51,760
Yes. Tremendous trouble.

200
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:55,518
Understood. If Ryo-sama says so,

201
00:12:55,568 --> 00:12:57,520
I'll never use this stupid strength again!

202
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,754
Good. Then if you use
that stupid strength again,

203
00:13:00,804 --> 00:13:03,560
you're out of here right away! Got it?

204
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:07,600
Understood, Ryo-sama.
I'll never use my stupid strength...

205
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:11,200
Cockroach!

206
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,720
I told you not to use that stupid strength!

207
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,480
I'm sorry, Ryo-sama.

208
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:22,780
But the cockroach...

209
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,480
I won't hear excuses! Get out right now!

210
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,840
Ryo-sama...

211
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:30,760
Don't you understand yet that everyone is
suffering because of your stupid strength?

212
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,720
When I say get out, you get out!

213
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,220
Understood.

214
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,840
He seems really depressed, somehow.

215
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:54,580
I wonder if the
"unwanted bride" plan didn't work out.

216
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:56,120
Is Maria here?

217
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,440
Yes, she's outside.

218
00:14:58,800 --> 00:14:59,980
Found you at last.

219
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:03,300
Maria-chan!

220
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,560
Reiko-san.

221
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,940
Could you help me for a moment?

222
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:08,160
Maria's here.

223
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:08,880
Thank goodness.

224
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,000
What is it?

225
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,880
This locker's gotten old,
so I want to move it.

226
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,700
It'd be easy for Maria-chan, wouldn't it?

227
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:16,840
Yes.

228
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,500
Heave...

229
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,460
I told you not to use your brute strength!

230
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,780
I can't do that...

231
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,120
Maria-chan...

232
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:43,100
How about it? If you pay attention,
it's a dead ringer, right?

233
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:44,620
She really does look just like him!

234
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,880
Yeah, you've got a good eye.

235
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:55,200
What's wrong with looking like that man? Watch your mouth.
This is Detective Otsuka from headquarters, narcotics unit.

236
00:15:55,200 --> 00:16:01,360
Narcotics investigator here. The wanted
drug dealer looks exactly like you.

237
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:09,320
We'd really like your cooperation with the investigation.
We want to catch them at the transaction site and wipe out the entire syndicate in one blow.

238
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:17,640
Listen carefully. This is a job only you can do, so count on you.
We'll fit you with a small transmitter, so we can check your location 24 hours a day.

239
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:32,440
The information we have is that JR's guard

240
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:35,780
The password is: say "Pancho,
" and they answer "Gonzales."

241
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:40,920
Pancho.

242
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,080
Gonzales.

243
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:53,600
Looks like we've made contact
with someone from the organization.

244
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:06,720
Boss, this is Mr. Yamashita,
the go-between this time.

245
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:07,580
Nice to meet you.

246
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,120
Well then, let's go.

247
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:12,940
Argh!

248
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:15,180
Hey, that guy.

249
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,820
Hey, go bring the car around.

250
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:18,280
Yeah.

251
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:20,200
About the other day...

252
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,720
Excuse me, Mr. Iguchi.
I have something to talk to you about.

253
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,140
Actually, the other day...

254
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:37,900
Hello?

255
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:42,620
Osaki.

256
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:50,940
By the way, Mr. Yamashita.

257
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:51,940
Yes.

258
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,740
What are you doing?

259
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,840
I knew it.
You're that Marley from back then.

260
00:17:58,300 --> 00:17:59,380
Too bad

261
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:02,980
I just got in touch with
the real Mr. Yamashita.

262
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,840
Damn it!

263
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:08,600
Shit. You idiot.

264
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:16,500
What is this crap?

265
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,700
Damn, we've been made?

266
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:26,680
The senior officer's in danger.
Let's move in.

267
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:28,800
No, we can't do that.

268
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:32,260
Orders from above are to catch them
at the deal scene no matter what.

269
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:45,520
I see, he really does look just like him.

270
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,120
What a fool.

271
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:52,580
From our investigation, these few places
are likely where the deal will happen.

272
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:55,180
Now we have no choice but to check them all,
one by one.

273
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,360
But if we move in a big way,
they'll spot us.

274
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,860
We'll search on our own, splitting up.

275
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:01,720
Understood?

276
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:02,520
Yes.

277
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:34,360
Maria-chan

278
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:40,020
Leo-sama is in danger?

279
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:43,460
I'm sure Ryo-chan will be fine, since it's him,
but...

280
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,440
True enough.

281
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,700
All that's left is to finish him off.

282
00:19:56,700 --> 00:20:00,020
No, let's rough him up a bit more first.

283
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,000
It's awfully quiet.

284
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:09,440
No good, Maria-chan.

285
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:11,500
No, you can't.

286
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,240
Ryo-sama hates it when
you use your brute strength.

287
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:15,960
I see.

288
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,260
Isn't it here?

289
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:22,480
What's this yarn?

290
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:24,540
This.

291
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,380
It's the sweater I knitted for Ryo-sama.

292
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:32,200
Ryo-sama wore it, didn't he?

293
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,000
Are you sure?

294
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:34,780
Yes.

295
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:37,760
Ryo-chan, trying to let us know

296
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:40,160
he unraveled the sweater
he wore under his jacket.

297
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,000
I heard a noise!

298
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,060
This woman!

299
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:25,020
Yamashita-san, are you satisfied now?

300
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:25,840
Well, sort of.

301
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:27,400
Boss!

302
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:29,920
What's wrong?

303
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,760
A woman with incredible
strength just burst in!

304
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:33,580
A woman?

305
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:36,440
We can't possibly beat her. Let's run!

306
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,720
Alright, we'll take her down one by one!

307
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:42,960
Ryo-sama...

308
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,140
Ryo-sama! Where are you?!

309
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:54,800
Master Ryo!

310
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:10,960
Please wait!

311
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:15,260
Don't come near!

312
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:19,320
One step closer and we throw this guy off!

313
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,360
Maria, fly the helicopter.

314
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:36,940
Maria.

315
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:44,840
Master Ryo, I'm sorry, I...

316
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:47,900
I used the brute strength
that Master Ryo hates.

317
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,080
Maria.

318
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:54,460
Maria, I permit it! Use your strength
to knock that helicopter down!

319
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:56,740
Lord Haideo!

320
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:22,200
Well done, Maria-chan.

321
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:26,220
The two of you look like
a perfect couple like that.

322
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:29,700
Reiko, you idiot, what are you saying?

323
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:33,520
Because Maria-chan was
really worried about Ryo-chan.

324
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:37,840
I'll never leave Ryo-sama again.

325
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:41,260
Maria-chan,
didn't you do great for Ryo-chan's sake?

326
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:43,580
The power of love really is strong,
isn't it.

327
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:48,120
That's right, mine isn't brute strength,
Ryo-sama, it's the power of love.

328
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:52,613
I've told you not to hug me,
get off, you're a man, you know.

329
00:23:52,663 --> 00:23:54,700
I don't have that kind of taste!

330
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:56,602
In the face of the power of love,

331
00:23:56,652 --> 00:23:59,580
That's a trivial matter!

332
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:01,980
It's not a trivial matter, you know!

333
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,800
Surprise and commotion,

334
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:25,400
miya-miya, please, please, whoa, predict

335
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:29,460
dede, decided, then a flash of inspiration

336
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:32,400
guyaa, bouncing along,
debe-debe, all wrapped up

337
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:33,920
crack-crack, into action

338
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:40,080
flying away, the most amazing power of all

339
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:52,420
everyone gather, come here,
the dreamlike final energy

340
00:24:53,400 --> 00:25:03,480
gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, painting the universe,
standing on the ground, the Kameari star spun round in a circle

341
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:08,600
That should be good enough, right?
Like hell it is!

342
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:24,960
Whoa, oh no, I've turned into a panda!

343
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:28,020
Another one of your schemes,
you cursed old geezer!

344
00:25:28,020 --> 00:25:30,360
I don't know if you're some
heaven police or whatever

345
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:33,520
Without that cane,
you're just a senile old man.

346
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:36,500
Next time:
Counterattack of the Cursed Old Geezer

347
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:37,940
I'll strike you back and beat you

